Wait updating trail: in getPose(p) we compute pose; while p between .28 and .5 record axe tip local. But character's torso rotation matters; store local pose + angle and compute tip. Easier compute world head tip after pose each frame and store world points, then draw trail in screen space. Let's do world coordinates. Need transform point.

Function torsoTransform(pose): hip (-? 0,-104), rotation lean. localToWorld(x,y):
```
const hx = 0, hy=-104;
const dx=x-hx, dy=y-hy;
const c=cos(pose.lean), s=sin(pose.lean);
return {x: charX + S*(hx + dx*c - dy*s), y: groundY + S*(hy + dx*s + dy*c)};
```
Axe head local: gripX + cos(angle)*96, gripY + sin(angle)*96. Get world via transform. Store every frame when swing and p between .24 and .56. Trail points {x,y,t}. Draw tapered segments with alpha by age.

Axe tip world also used impact? Impact at stump top fixed.

Draw order in render:
